Subject: [PATCH 1/2] refactor(ui): seen query, icon-button classes, journal,
 party, companions, campaigns, transfers, cookbook

The other UI (R1.5.13-R1.5.23), behaviour-preserving. seenQuery builds every poll's seen query in
the table's order (party, companion, notes, cookbook adopt it; the table's is F-b's), and the
notes, party and cookbook polls back off through retryDelay. JOURNAL_ICON_BUTTON and
HEADER_ICON_BUTTON compose today's class strings unchanged. Each .tsx of V2's now exports one
component: the transfers' JSX hooks are .ts with a *-dialogs.tsx each, their control factories
.ts files with createElement, MoveForm a useMoveForm hook over pure rules; the journal's Journal
composes useJournalLayout, useSaid, useFocusTo, useReaderPick and useOrdering over utils/reader,
Sortable useSortableDrag, NoteEditor's two hooks their own files, use-notes a local useBookReads;
the campaigns' index useCampaignIndexNav and useCampaignChoice, its card's words feature-words;
seat-urls holds the encoded seat paths (take-controls and three pages); the props types are in
types.ts files. use-transfers follows through useFollow, its body and the party page's with
NO_DICE in today's key order.

Gates: the L1 of this tree is green: jest 306 suites, 9,695 tests, 0 red; typegen, tsc clean;
eslint 0 errors, 480 warnings (661 at the base of the lane); gates 1-12 ok, gate 12 down to 2
cycle groups (the transfers pair gone). V2's product warnings fall from 196 to 15: rule (a) 106
to 3 (campaign-status, page-toast: left for Phase 4), named types 70 to 0, cognitive complexity
over 15 4 to 0, react-hooks 16 to 12. No disable added; three directives given reasons.

